1
00:00:11,590 --> 00:00:12,870
Hi, Michelle.

2
00:00:12,870 --> 00:00:13,900
Hello, Harry.

3
00:00:13,900 --> 00:00:15,480
It's nice to see you again.

4
00:00:15,480 --> 00:00:16,550
Hello.

5
00:00:16,550 --> 00:00:18,260
Hi, Susan.

6
00:00:18,260 --> 00:00:20,620
We have both been excited about seeing you

7
00:00:20,620 --> 00:00:22,600
and having lunch with you today.

8
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:24,610
Michelle picked these flowers out for you.

9
00:00:24,610 --> 00:00:28,060
Daddy, can we go soon?

10
00:00:28,060 --> 00:00:30,400
We're going to go to lunch in a few minutes, honey.

11
00:00:30,400 --> 00:00:32,810
But I'm thirsty.

12
00:00:32,810 --> 00:00:37,640
OK. You go out and get a drink of water at the fountain.

13
00:00:37,640 --> 00:00:39,270
The fountain is over there, Michelle.

14
00:00:39,270 --> 00:00:40,690
Near the Exit sign.

15
00:00:40,690 --> 00:00:48,550
Thank you.

16
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:51,300
Michelle is a little shy.

17
00:00:51,300 --> 00:00:54,830
I used to be that way when I was her age.

18
00:00:54,830 --> 00:00:57,610
Harry, if Michelle doesn't want to go,

19
00:00:57,610 --> 00:00:59,100
we don't have to.

20
00:00:59,100 --> 00:01:00,220
She'll be fine.

21
00:01:00,220 --> 00:01:00,850
Remember,

22
00:01:00,850 --> 00:01:04,130
I haven't dated any one else since her mother died.

23
00:01:04,130 --> 00:01:06,720
This is a little difficult for her.

24
00:01:06,720 --> 00:01:07,790
Are you ready to go?

25
00:01:07,790 --> 00:01:10,890
Yes. But could you wait one minute?

26
00:01:10,890 --> 00:01:12,670
I have a call to make.

27
00:01:12,670 --> 00:01:19,020
Would you excuse me?

28
00:01:19,020 --> 00:01:21,670
Sam, get Mr. Levine at Toytown Stores

29
00:01:21,670 --> 00:01:23,130
on the telephone for me, please.

30
00:01:23,130 --> 00:01:30,060
Right.

31
00:01:30,060 --> 00:01:33,000
Hello. Susan Stewart calling Mr. Levine, please.

32
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:37,300
He's on the phone.

33
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:40,620
Mr. Levine, Susan Stewart.

34
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:43,920
I find myself in an embarrassing situation.

35
00:01:43,920 --> 00:01:46,080
I made another lunch date for today

36
00:01:46,080 --> 00:01:49,410
and forgot to enter it in my appointment book.

37
00:01:49,410 --> 00:01:52,600
Can you and I meet for drinks tomorrow?

38
00:01:52,600 --> 00:01:57,470
I'd really appreciate it.... Yes.... Thank you....

39
00:01:57,470 --> 00:02:00,130
Tomorrow at five o'clock at the Biltmore.

40
00:02:00,130 --> 00:02:01,200
I'll see you then.

41
00:02:01,200 --> 00:02:27,730
Thank you, Mr. Levine.

42
00:02:27,730 --> 00:02:29,430
Welcome to the South Street restaurant, folks.

43
00:02:29,430 --> 00:02:30,310
What'll it be?

44
00:02:30,310 --> 00:02:31,450
What do you recommend?

45
00:02:31,450 --> 00:02:33,430
Well, the crab salad's always a big hit.

46
00:02:33,430 --> 00:02:34,900
Susan, would you like the crab salad?

47
00:02:34,900 --> 00:02:36,810
I'd love the crab salad.

48
00:02:36,810 --> 00:02:38,870
Michelle, would you like to try the crab salad, too?

49
00:02:38,870 --> 00:02:40,230
OK, Daddy.

50
00:02:40,230 --> 00:02:42,070
We'll have three crab salads

51
00:02:42,070 --> 00:02:44,000
and a pitcher of lemonade.

52
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:48,220
Help yourself to celery and carrots and other vegetables.

53
00:02:48,220 --> 00:02:49,810
We used to catch crabs.

54
00:02:49,810 --> 00:02:51,060
Where was that?

55
00:02:51,060 --> 00:02:53,110
We had a summer house on Fire Island.

56
00:02:53,110 --> 00:02:54,420
Do you remember, Michelle?

57
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:54,970
Sure.

58
00:02:54,970 --> 00:02:57,330
You and Mommy used to take me on the ferryboat.

59
00:02:57,330 --> 00:02:58,860
Sometimes, at night,

60
00:02:58,860 --> 00:03:01,150
we would go down to the beach and catch crabs,

61
00:03:01,150 --> 00:03:02,480
remember?

62
00:03:02,480 --> 00:03:04,410
With a piece of meat on a string!

63
00:03:04,410 --> 00:03:05,330
Right.

64
00:03:05,330 --> 00:03:21,330
Well, I think I'm going to go get us all some vegetables.

65
00:03:21,330 --> 00:03:22,890
There you go.

66
00:03:22,890 --> 00:03:31,000
Thank you.

67
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,080
And some ice-cold lemonade.

68
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:34,760
Thank you.

69
00:03:34,760 --> 00:03:40,670
Enjoy it.

70
00:03:40,670 --> 00:03:43,640
Michelle, can I help you with the lemonade?

71
00:03:43,640 --> 00:03:44,310
No, thank you.

72
00:03:44,310 --> 00:03:48,840
I'll wait for my father.

73
00:03:48,840 --> 00:03:50,980
Michelle, can we have a talk?

74
00:03:50,980 --> 00:03:52,940
Sure.

75
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:54,690
I know you miss your mother.

76
00:03:54,690 --> 00:03:55,850
You do?

77
00:03:55,850 --> 00:03:59,860
Yes. And I'm not trying to take her place.

78
00:03:59,860 --> 00:04:01,640
Then why are you and Daddy

79
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:03,960
spending so much time together?

80
00:04:03,960 --> 00:04:06,090
Because we like each other.

81
00:04:06,090 --> 00:04:09,250
And right now, he needs a friend.

82
00:04:09,250 --> 00:04:10,460
I'm his friend.

83
00:04:10,460 --> 00:04:13,790
I know you are.

84
00:04:13,790 --> 00:04:16,780
Sometimes he's very sad.

85
00:04:16,780 --> 00:04:18,970
And so are you, I think.

86
00:04:18,970 --> 00:04:21,390
Sometimes.

87
00:04:21,390 --> 00:04:25,370
I'd like to be your friend, too.

88
00:04:25,370 --> 00:04:33,530
Will you let me be your friend, Michelle?

89
00:04:33,530 --> 00:04:36,970
So, what were you two talking about?

90
00:04:36,970 --> 00:04:38,600
Just girl talk, Daddy.

91
00:04:38,600 --> 00:04:40,610
It's too hard to explain.

92
00:04:40,610 --> 00:04:41,600
You're probably right.

93
00:04:41,600 --> 00:04:44,600
Well, let's get started.
